<title>NETHERLANDS: Commercial Union's Delta Lloyd '96 net up 11.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union's Delta Lloyd '96 net up 11.3 pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>AMSTERDAM, Feb 26 (reuter) - Year to dec 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit					327.9   vs 294.5</p>
<p>    Net profit per share (guilders)	    99.38  vs  89.24</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)			    49.73  vs  44.73</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit from normal operations   491.0   vs 398.7</p>
<p>    Taxes					     131.3   vs 104.2</p>
<p>    Extraordinary post-tax charge		 31.8  vs nil</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)			     5.18  vs   4.86</p>
<p>Note -- Delta Lloyd verzekeringsgroep NV is a fully-owned subsidiary of Commercial Union Assurance Co Plc.</p>
<p>Breakdown of pre-tax profit from normal operations:</p>
<p>    - Life insurance				363     vs 304</p>
<p>    - Non-life business			    61     vs  50</p>
<p>    - Holding company activities		 54     vs  37</p>
<p>    - Others					   13     vs   8</p>
<p>Breakdown of turnover:</p>
<p>    - Premium income life ins. (billion)	2.00  vs   1.81</p>
<p>    - Premium income non-life (billion)	 1.08  vs   1.04</p>
<p>    - Other activities			     23.3   vs  18.6</p>
<p>    - Investment income (billion)		 2.07  vs   1.99</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
